            new GossipText(282, 120, "They're dead, they don't care...\n\n<$NPC$ sighs in fatigue>\n\nIt didn't use to be this way. \nI feel like we're losing our way as a people."),
            new GossipText(283, 121, "<$NPC$ is quietly grieving>"),
            new GossipText(284, 122, "The name's $NPC$, I'm a butcher. \nIt's good to see a friendly face.\n\nWell, what'll it be?"),
            new GossipText(285, 123, "<$NPC$ is preoccupied and pays you no attention>"),
            new GossipText(286, 124, "Swords, axes, shields, armor...\nAll in high demand these days.\n\nThe market of St. Revere use to be very different.\n\n<$NPC$ sighs>\n\nA sign of the times, I suppose."),
            new GossipText(287, 125, "$NPC$'s the name, $class$. I'm a businessman, plain as. An entrepreneur of sorts. My caravan brings goods into St. Revere from the west.\n\n<$NPC$ is notably tired>\n\nI've made a fortune lately, but the demand is tough to keep up with. Hard to believe that of all places, St. Revere was sitting on so much coin."),
            new GossipText(288, 126, "Well, it's just... don't you find it strange?\n\nSt. Revere for years has been the envy of this island of ours... never knew how you guys did it. 'Faith! Praise the Lords!', or so it goes. \n\nA peaceful place like this suddenly buying up every sword and shield in sight? Hiring every mercenary that walks into town? \n\nWhat changed, and where's the gold come from?"),
            new GossipText(289, 127, "Beats me. But, money talks.\n\n<$NPC$ pauses to think>\n\nI couldn't say for sure exactly how many other caravans come and go... but I wouldn't be surprised if these folk have bought enough armaments to raise an army.\n\n<$NPC$ shrugs>"),
            new GossipText(290, 130, "Students gifted with a keen intellect and unwavering discipline may walk the path of the mage. The arcane magic available to magi is both great and dangerous, and thus is revealed only to the most devoted practitioners."),
            new GossipText(291, 131, "Clerics are devoted to the spiritual, and we express our unwavering faith by serving the people. \n\nFor millennia we have left behind the confines of the church to support our allies in war-torn lands. In the midst of terrible conflict, no hero questions the value of our priestly order."),
            new GossipText(292, 133, "Yes, what business have you?"),
            new GossipText(293, 134, "Now see here, $class$ - if you want the latest news than simply tend to the Town Cryer downtown.\n\nRun along now."),
            new GossipText(294, 135, "Vincent? What about him?"),
            new GossipText(295, 136, "<$NPC$ appears caught off guard>\n\nThat Vincent... let me tell you something, little $G=boy:girl$. That is none of your concern."),
            new GossipText(296, 137, "Well certainly, we owe a great deal to sir Zedek.\n\nWithout him, we'd be lost. \nA wealthy philanthropist such as himself is a gift from the Gods, no doubt."),
            new GossipText(304, 190, "No coin, no barter. Put your gold away, traveler. What kind of servant would I be if I charged for what was given to me by grace? The Lord provides, I'm just the vessel.\n\nNow, what can I reshape for you?"),
            new GossipText(297, 200, "<The man glares at you>"),
            new GossipText(298, 201, "My name is $NPC$ and as you can see,\n\n<He gestures at the house>\n\nThis is my home."),
            new GossipText(299, 202, "And?"),
            new GossipText(300, 203, "You'll not ask again... noted."),
            new GossipText(302, 204, "<$NPC$ rubs his hands together>\n\nAh, another fine $CLASS$...\nHow may I be of service?"),
            new GossipText(303, 300, "Queue solo or with a partner for 2v2 arena battles. Matchmaking pairs fighters of similar rating. Victories increase your rating while defeats lower it. Beating stronger opponents earns more points. Losing to weaker ones costs more. Climb the ranks and prove yourself."),
            new GossipText(305, 400, "You're probably wondering why I'm here.\nSo am I, frankly.\n\nWell then, what will it be?"),
